+//
+// LLAMA_EXPERT_PAD=1: a GGUF aligns tensor data to 32 bytes, so an expert tensor whose file offset is
+// not a multiple of EC_DIRECT_ALIGN (Qwen3.5-122B-A10B: every one) had every read staged and copied
+// (the console: ~0.9 GB/s staged against ~2 GB/s in place). Its slots are then EC_DIRECT_ALIGN apart
+// beyond the expert's bytes (nb[2] = nb[1]*ne[1] + EC_DIRECT_ALIGN, which the MUL_MAT_ID kernels
+// take as the expert stride) and the tensor's data is moved, when bound, to the file offset's
+// remainder: the aligned span around an expert, or around any aligned part of it, then lands in
+// place, spilling only into the gap before and after its slot (a part's spill is the same file
+// bytes its neighbouring parts write there)
